From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0046] meson-ir: software decoder programs the input filter itself

BL301 reprograms this decoder for its hardware-NEC wake detection during deep suspend and
leaves REG0 FILTER=3; meson_ir_sw_decoder_init() only set BASE_TIME, so after every resume
the raw decoder ran with the weaker glitch filter (measured: 70fa0009 -> 30fa0009). The
filter is now set explicitly (7, the bootloader value on this board) at init and resume.
Verified with timer-woken cycles: REG0 back to 70fa0009 after resume. Physical remote
key-up timing after resume: see the 25.09 report.

---
diff -ruN b/drivers/media/rc/meson-ir.c c/drivers/media/rc/meson-ir.c
--- a/drivers/media/rc/meson-ir.c
+++ b/drivers/media/rc/meson-ir.c
@@ -94,6 +94,12 @@
 #define IRQSEL_RISE				3
 
 #define MESON_RAW_TRATE				10	/* us */
+/*
+ * h96 0046: input glitch filter for raw decoding. The bootloader leaves 7 on
+ * this board; BL301 sets 3 for its hardware-NEC wake detection and does not
+ * restore it, so the raw decoder must program it itself (init and resume).
+ */
+#define MESON_RAW_FILTER			7
 #define MESON_HW_TRATE				20	/* us */
 
 /**
@@ -498,10 +504,11 @@
 				   FIELD_PREP(IR_DEC_REG2_MODE,
 					      DEC_MODE_RAW));
 
-	/* Set rate */
-	regmap_update_bits(ir->reg, IR_DEC_REG0, IR_DEC_REG0_BASE_TIME,
-			   FIELD_PREP(IR_DEC_REG0_BASE_TIME,
-				      MESON_RAW_TRATE - 1));
+	/* Set rate and input filter */
+	regmap_update_bits(ir->reg, IR_DEC_REG0,
+			   IR_DEC_REG0_BASE_TIME | IR_DEC_REG0_FILTER,
+			   FIELD_PREP(IR_DEC_REG0_BASE_TIME, MESON_RAW_TRATE - 1) |
+			   FIELD_PREP(IR_DEC_REG0_FILTER, MESON_RAW_FILTER));
 	/* IRQ on rising and falling edges */
 	regmap_update_bits(ir->reg, IR_DEC_REG1, IR_DEC_REG1_IRQSEL,
 			   FIELD_PREP(IR_DEC_REG1_IRQSEL, IRQSEL_RISE_FALL));
